---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Sales Tax Calculator – Calculate Tax, Total Price & Reverse Sales Tax"
  description="Calculate sales tax, total purchase cost, or the original price before tax using a custom or selected tax rate."
  category="Finance"
  calculatorName="Sales Tax Calculator"
  slug="sales-tax-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'sales tax calculator',
    'reverse sales tax calculator',
    'nj sales tax calculator',
    'california sales tax calculator',
    'nyc sales tax calculator',
    'missouri sales tax calculator',
    'car sales tax calculator',
    'ohio sales tax calculator',
    'mn sales tax calculator',
    'ny sales tax calculator'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- CALCULATION MODE SELECTOR TABS -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 hidden sm:inline">
          Mode:
        </span>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-1.5 w-full sm:w-auto text-xs font-bold">
          <button type="button" class="btn-st-mode active rounded-xl border border-blue-600 bg-blue-50 px-4 py-2 text-blue-700 dark:border-blue-500 dark:bg-blue-950/60 dark:text-blue-300 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="add">
            ➕ Add Sales Tax
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-st-mode rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="reverse">
            🔄 Reverse Sales Tax
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-st-mode rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="car">
            🚗 Car Sales Tax
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN CALCULATOR FORM CONTAINER -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/30 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20 sm:p-7">
      
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🏷️</span> Sales Tax Calculator
        </h2>
        <p id="txt-st-subtitle" class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Calculate sales tax amount and total purchase cost using a custom or state estimated tax rate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <form id="form-sales-tax" class="mt-4 space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
        
        <!-- SECTION 1: PRICE & TAX RATE INPUTS -->
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-white/70 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>💵</span> 1. Purchase Amount & Tax Rate
            </span>
            <span id="badge-st-location" class="text-[11px] font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/60 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-md border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-900/50">
              Custom Rate Applied
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <!-- Amount Input (Dynamic Label) -->
            <div>
              <label for="inp-st-amount" id="lbl-st-amount" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Price Before Tax ($ / ₹)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-st-amount" value="1000" step="10" min="0" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="1,000" />
            </div>

            <!-- Tax Rate Input -->
            <div>
              <label for="inp-st-rate" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Sales Tax Rate (% percentage)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-st-rate" value="7.25" step="0.05" min="0" max="40" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="7.25" />
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Location Presets Dropdown & Quick Buttons -->
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2">
              <label for="sel-st-location" class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                State & City Estimated Rate Presets:
              </label>
              <select id="sel-st-location" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer">
                <option value="custom" selected>Custom Tax Rate (Manual)</option>
                <option value="ca">California Estimate (7.25% Base)</option>
                <option value="nj">New Jersey Estimate (6.625% Statewide)</option>
                <option value="ny">New York State (4.00% Base)</option>
                <option value="nyc">New York City (8.875% Combined)</option>
                <option value="mo">Missouri Estimate (4.225% Base)</option>
                <option value="oh">Ohio Estimate (5.75% Base)</option>
                <option value="mn">Minnesota Estimate (6.875% Base)</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            <!-- Quick Preset Badges -->
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[11px]">
              <span class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold mr-1">Quick Select:</span>
              <button type="button" class="btn-st-loc-badge rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2 py-0.5 font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-loc="ca" data-rate="7.25">California (7.25%)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-st-loc-badge rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2 py-0.5 font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-loc="nj" data-rate="6.625">New Jersey (6.625%)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-st-loc-badge rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2 py-0.5 font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-loc="nyc" data-rate="8.875">NYC (8.875%)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-st-loc-badge rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2 py-0.5 font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-loc="mo" data-rate="4.225">Missouri (4.225%)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-st-loc-badge rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2 py-0.5 font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-loc="oh" data-rate="5.75">Ohio (5.75%)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-st-loc-badge rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2 py-0.5 font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-loc="mn" data-rate="6.875">Minnesota (6.875%)</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 2: CAR SALES TAX SPECIFIC INPUTS (Visible in Car Mode only) -->
        <div id="sec-st-car-inputs" class="hidden rounded-2xl border border-blue-200/80 bg-blue-50/40 p-4 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-blue-950/20 space-y-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>🚗</span> 2. Vehicle Trade-In, Rebates & Taxable Fees
          </span>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-st-tradein" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Trade-In Allowance ($ / ₹)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-st-tradein" value="5000" step="500" min="0" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="5,000" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="inp-st-rebate" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Manufacturer Rebates / Discount</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-st-rebate" value="1500" step="250" min="0" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="1,500" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="inp-st-fees" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Taxable Documentation / Fees</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-st-fees" value="500" step="50" min="0" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="500" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 italic">
            * Note: Taxable treatment of trade-in credits, manufacturer rebates, and dealer doc fees varies by jurisdiction.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- ACTION BUTTONS -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2">
          <button type="submit" id="btn-calc-st" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">
            Calculate Sales Tax →
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-clear-st" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer">
            Clear All (✕)
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- ACCESSIBLE ERROR -->
        <p id="err-st" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-2.5 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

      </form>

      <!-- RESULTS PRESENTATION SECTION (Hidden initially) -->
      <div id="st-results-section" class="hidden mt-6 space-y-6">
        
        <!-- 1. MAIN RESULT HERO CARD -->
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-blue-200 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-blue-50/40 to-blue-100/50 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-blue-500/5 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-blue-950/30 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-blue-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
            <div>
              <span id="lbl-st-hero-title" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">TOTAL PRICE INCLUDING TAX</span>
              <div id="res-st-hero-amount" class="mt-1 text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">$ 1,072.50</div>
              <div id="res-st-hero-subtitle" class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Calculated using 7.25% Sales Tax Rate</div>
            </div>
            <div class="sm:text-right">
              <span id="lbl-st-hero-secondary" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Sales Tax Amount:</span>
              <div id="res-st-hero-secondary" class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">+ $ 72.50</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="grid-st-summary" class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div id="lbl-st-grid-1" class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Price Before Tax</div>
              <div id="res-st-grid-1" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">$ 1,000.00</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Effective Tax Rate</div>
              <div id="res-st-grid-2" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">7.25%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Tax Amount</div>
              <div id="res-st-grid-3" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">$ 72.50</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div id="lbl-st-grid-4" class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Total Cost</div>
              <div id="res-st-grid-4" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">$ 1,072.50</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. STEP-BY-STEP CALCULATION BREAKDOWN -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-2 border-b border-slate-200 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>📐</span> Sales Tax Calculation Breakdown
            </h3>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono" id="txt-st-formula-name">
              Standard Sales Tax Formula
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/40 space-y-2 text-xs font-mono">
            <div class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Formula: <strong id="txt-st-breakdown-formula" class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">Tax = Price × (Rate ÷ 100)</strong></div>
            <div class="pt-1 border-t border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800">
              <div>Step 1: <span id="txt-st-breakdown-step1" class="font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">$1,000.00 × 0.0725 = $72.50 Sales Tax</span></div>
              <div class="mt-1">Step 2: <span id="txt-st-breakdown-step2" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">$1,000.00 + $72.50 = $1,072.50 Total Cost</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. TAX RATE COMPARISON TABLE & PDF DOWNLOAD -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 mb-2">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <span>📊</span> Tax Rate Comparison
              </h3>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                Compare your purchase across different state and local sales tax percentages.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Download PDF Button -->
            <button type="button" id="btn-st-download-pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer" title="Download calculation as PDF">
              <span>📄</span> <span id="txt-btn-st-pdf">Download PDF</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-2.5 rounded-l-lg">Sales Tax Rate</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right">Tax Amount</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right rounded-r-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Total Price</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="tbl-st-comparison" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
                <!-- Injected dynamically -->
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATIONAL CONTENT SLOT -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="st-content">
      
      <!-- 1. HOW TO USE THE CALCULATOR -->
      <h2>How to Use the Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Calculating sales tax, estimating total checkout costs, or determining pre-tax prices is straightforward:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Choose your calculation mode:</strong> Select <em>Add Sales Tax</em> (to add tax to a net price), <em>Reverse Sales Tax</em> (to extract tax from a gross price), or <em>Car Sales Tax</em> (to factor in vehicle trade-ins and rebates).</li>
        <li><strong>Enter the purchase price or total amount:</strong> Type the monetary amount in dollars or your local currency.</li>
        <li><strong>Select a location estimate or enter a custom tax rate:</strong> Choose a state preset (e.g. California, New Jersey, New York City) or input your exact municipal percentage.</li>
        <li><strong>Add trade-in, rebate, discount, or taxable fees if using the vehicle calculator:</strong> Deduct eligible credits to reach the net taxable car amount.</li>
        <li><strong>Click Calculate Sales Tax:</strong> Review your itemized sales tax amount, total price, and step-by-step mathematical breakdown.</li>
        <li><strong>Review the tax rate comparison matrix:</strong> Compare the impact of various tax percentages on your purchase.</li>
        <li><strong>Download the calculation as a PDF:</strong> Save a branded PDF report for your personal budgeting or bookkeeping records.</li>
      </ol>

      <!-- 2. REVERSE SALES TAX CALCULATOR SECTION -->
      <h2>Reverse Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>reverse sales tax calculator</strong> enables consumers and accountants to find the original pre-tax price from a tax-inclusive receipt total. Rather than incorrectly subtracting a flat percentage from the final amount, reverse sales tax uses division:
      </p>
      <p>
        <code>Original Price Before Tax = Total Price ÷ (1 + Tax Rate / 100)</code>
      </p>
      <p>
        For example, if you paid <strong>$107.00</strong> at a <strong>7%</strong> sales tax rate, dividing $107 by 1.07 yields an exact base price of <strong>$100.00</strong>, with <strong>$7.00</strong> in sales tax. Actual transaction totals may differ slightly due to penny-rounding rules at the item level.
      </p>

      <!-- 3. SALES TAX CALCULATION EXAMPLE -->
      <h2>Sales Tax Calculation Example</h2>
      <p>
        Consider a standard retail purchase of $1,000 at a 7.25% combined sales tax rate:
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-1.5 font-mono">
        <div>Purchase Price (Pre-Tax): <strong>$1,000.00</strong></div>
        <div>Sales Tax Rate: <strong>7.25%</strong></div>
        <div class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold">Sales Tax Amount: $1,000.00 × 0.0725 = $72.50</div>
        <div class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-bold">Total Price: $1,000.00 + $72.50 = $1,072.50</div>
        <div class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 pt-1 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          Reverse Check: $1,072.50 ÷ 1.0725 = $1,000.00 Base Price ($72.50 Tax)
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
        * This example is for illustration. Actual tax liabilities can vary based on local district taxes, product taxability exemptions, and point-of-sale rounding.
      </p>

      <!-- 4. CALIFORNIA SALES TAX SECTION -->
      <h2>California Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        When estimating purchases in the Golden State, using a <strong>california sales tax calculator</strong> helps you account for both state and local district levies. California maintains a statewide base sales tax rate of 7.25% (composed of 6.00% state tax and 1.25% mandatory local county/city operational funds).
      </p>
      <p>
        Because local special tax districts (such as transportation authorities) add supplementary percentages, total effective sales tax rates in California cities typically range between <strong>7.75% and 10.75%</strong> (e.g., Los Angeles and San Francisco).
      </p>

      <!-- 5. NEW JERSEY SALES TAX SECTION -->
      <h2>NJ Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Shoppers in the Garden State frequently search for an <strong>nj sales tax calculator</strong> to forecast retail costs. New Jersey operates a uniform statewide sales tax rate of <strong>6.625%</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unlike many other states, New Jersey generally does not permit additional county or municipal sales taxes. Furthermore, qualifying retail businesses located in designated Urban Enterprise Zones (UEZ) charge a reduced sales tax rate of <strong>3.3125%</strong>, and clothing and most unprepared groceries are exempt from sales tax statewide.
      </p>

      <!-- 6. NEW YORK AND NYC SALES TAX -->
      <h2>NY and NYC Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        In New York, sales tax is composed of state-level, county-level, and municipal rates. Utilizing an <strong>ny sales tax calculator</strong> or a dedicated <strong>nyc sales tax calculator</strong> helps clarify these regional differences:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>New York State:</strong> The base statewide sales tax rate is <strong>4.00%</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>New York City (NYC):</strong> Purchases in the five boroughs incur a combined sales tax rate of <strong>8.875%</strong> (4.00% NY State + 4.50% NYC City + 0.375% Metropolitan Commuter Transportation District surcharge).</li>
        <li><strong>Upstate & Long Island Counties:</strong> Total combined sales tax rates across New York counties generally range between <strong>7.00% and 8.875%</strong>.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 7. MISSOURI SALES TAX CALCULATOR -->
      <h2>Missouri Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        In Missouri, the state base sales tax is <strong>4.225%</strong>. Using our <strong>missouri sales tax calculator</strong> allows you to input your exact municipal rate because local city, county, and special transportation development districts (TDDs) frequently raise the combined tax rate between <strong>6.00% and 10.00%+</strong> (e.g., in St. Louis and Kansas City).
      </p>

      <!-- 8. OHIO SALES TAX CALCULATOR -->
      <h2>Ohio Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Our <strong>ohio sales tax calculator</strong> estimates retail purchases across the Buckeye State. Ohio sets a base state sales tax of <strong>5.75%</strong>, with individual county "piggyback" taxes and regional transit authority levies bringing total rates between <strong>6.50% and 8.00%</strong> (e.g., 8.00% in Cuyahoga County).
      </p>

      <!-- 9. MINNESOTA SALES TAX CALCULATOR -->
      <h2>MN Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Using an <strong>mn sales tax calculator</strong> helps Minnesota shoppers budget effectively. Minnesota assesses a statewide sales tax rate of <strong>6.875%</strong>. In cities like Minneapolis and St. Paul, additional municipal and transit taxes result in combined rates between <strong>7.50% and 9.00%+</strong>, while essential clothing and prescription drugs remain exempt from state sales tax.
      </p>

      <!-- 10. CAR SALES TAX CALCULATOR CONTENT -->
      <h2>Car Sales Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Automotive purchases involve substantial transactions where sales tax represents thousands of dollars. Using a specialized <strong>car sales tax calculator</strong> helps buyers understand how trade-in vehicles, manufacturer rebates, and dealer document fees impact taxable amounts:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Trade-In Tax Credit:</strong> In most US states, the value of a traded-in vehicle is subtracted from the purchase price before sales tax is calculated (e.g., a $30,000 car with a $10,000 trade-in is taxed only on $20,000).</li>
        <li><strong>Manufacturer Rebates:</strong> In many jurisdictions, manufacturer cash-back rebates are considered customer cash down payments and do not reduce the taxable vehicle amount.</li>
        <li><strong>Taxable Dealer Fees:</strong> Documentation and delivery fees are frequently subject to sales tax, while government registration and title fees are generally non-taxable.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 11. COMMON MISTAKES -->
      <h2>Common Mistakes When Calculating Sales Tax</h2>

      <h3>Using the Wrong Tax Rate</h3>
      <p>
        Relying solely on the state base rate without factoring in local municipal, county, and transit district surcharges leads to underestimating checkout totals.
      </p>

      <h3>Adding Tax to an Already Tax-Inclusive Price</h3>
      <p>
        If an invoice or receipt total already includes sales tax, adding another percentage overcharges the buyer. Use the reverse calculation mode to extract the pre-tax base.
      </p>

      <h3>Ignoring Taxable Fees</h3>
      <p>
        Shipping, handling, processing, and dealer doc fees are often subject to sales tax depending on state regulations.
      </p>

      <h3>Assuming Every Product Is Taxed the Same Way</h3>
      <p>
        Many states exempt essential groceries, prescription medications, or apparel from sales tax, while taxing luxury goods and electronics at standard rates.
      </p>

      <h3>Ignoring Rounding</h3>
      <p>
        Point-of-sale cash registers compute tax per line item or on total invoice amounts using standard rounding rules (half-cent up), which may cause one-cent discrepancies.
      </p>

      <!-- 12. IMPORTANT ASSUMPTIONS AND DISCLAIMER -->
      <h2>Important Information and Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Please keep the following principles in mind when reviewing your sales tax calculation results:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mathematical Simulation:</strong> Calculations apply standard percentage formulas based on the exact rate entered.</li>
        <li><strong>Estimates Not Legal Advice:</strong> State and municipal tax rates change periodically through legislative updates. This calculator provides planning estimates and does not represent official tax advisory services or government tax certification.</li>
        <li><strong>Exemptions & Special Rules:</strong> Non-profit organizations, resale certificate holders, and exempt product categories should consult state departments of revenue for formal filing guidelines.</li>
      </ul>

    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- FAQ SECTION SLOT (EXACTLY 7 FAQs AS REQUIRED) -->
  <Fragment slot="faq">
