      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800" open>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            1. What is a sales tax calculator?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          A sales tax calculator is a financial tool that computes the tax added to retail purchases, the total price including tax, or the original pre-tax price from a tax-inclusive total using custom or regional tax rates.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            2. How do I calculate sales tax?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          To calculate sales tax, multiply the pre-tax item price by the sales tax rate expressed as a decimal (e.g. $100 × 0.07 for 7% tax = $7.00 tax). Then add the tax to the base price to get the final total ($107.00).
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            3. How does a reverse sales tax calculator work?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Reverse sales tax calculates the original pre-tax price by dividing the total price by (1 + Tax Rate / 100). For example, a $107 total with 7% tax is divided by 1.07, revealing a base price of $100 and a tax amount of $7.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            4. Can I use this calculator for California or New Jersey sales tax?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
